<title>RUSSIA: Mosenergo 1996 shr $0.23 vs $0.16.</title>
<headline>Mosenergo 1996 shr $0.23 vs $0.16.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>    (million US dollars)	   1996	 1995</p>
<p>    Total operating revenues    4,134	2,929</p>
<p>    Operating income		1,104	  653</p>
<p>    Net income			  598	  383</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (dollars)  0.23	 0.16</p>
<p>NOTES - Full name OAO Energetiki i Elektrifikatsii Mosenergo. Figures audited by Arthur Andersen in accordance with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). Figures supplied by Salomon Bros.</p>
<p>Company previously announced 1996 net profit of 2.80 trillion roubles on a Russian accounts cash basis after 2.45 trillion in 1995, on sales of 14.87 trillion on a cash basis or 21.90 trillion on an accruals basis in 1996 after 9.89 trillion on a cash basis in 1995.</p>
<p>Unified Energy System (UES)  EESR.RTS owns 49 percent of Mosenergo.</p>
<p>Mosenergo has issued American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) and is planning to issue a Eurobond this summer through Salomon Bros. Earlier on Monday Standard &amp; Poor's rated Mosenergo BB-, the same rating as that of the Russian Federation.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
